From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:18:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: keys typed faster than the frames come keep their
 order

Problem: when several keys arrive in one frame (a quick typist on a
slow machine, or a port that draws on the CPU), typing on a selected
cell started the edit with the first character and dropped the rest
of the frame's events, and the cell editor took Enter, Tab, Escape
and arrows from anywhere in that frame. "123" then Enter left 1 in
the cell; "1", Enter, "2" lost the 2; an Escape before the typing
cancelled it.

Fix: a frame now takes keyboard events up to the first key that is
not typing (an editing, moving or function key, a shortcut, a
clipboard command); the rest wait for the next frame, in order, as
if typed more slowly. The frame that opens the editor gives it all
the text typed in it. While the Python code editor is open, which
already reads a frame's keys in order, frames are not split.

Scope: crates/ui-egui (SheetApp::logic pacing, the grid's keyboard
input in grid/keyboard.rs).

Tests: tests/type_to_edit_one_frame.rs, 12 tests. 10 of them fail
without this change (the other two cover Shift+Space and typing into
an editor that is already open).
